# GraphQL API Rules (operation list: docs/05-API-OPERATIONS.md)

## Stack
- `graphql-yoga` mounted in Fastify at `POST /graphql` (GET disabled except in dev for GraphiQL).
- `@pothos/core` code-first schema + `@pothos/plugin-scope-auth` (+ `plugin-validation`/zod is NOT
  used for business validation — services validate with Zod). No Pothos Prisma plugin: resolvers
  return service DTOs.
- Schema SDL is exported to `schema.graphql` by `pnpm schema:print` and committed; CI fails if it is stale.

## Naming
- Types `PascalCase`, fields `camelCase`, enums `SCREAMING_SNAKE` (mirror Prisma enums).
- Queries are nouns (`civicCard`, `office`, `myCorrections`); mutations are verb-first
  (`saveLocation`, `submitCorrection`, `sendAlert`). Admin operations are prefixed `admin` for
  queries (`adminOffices`) and use verbs for mutations (`upsertOffice`, `retireOffice`).
- One input object per mutation: `mutation saveLocation(input: SaveLocationInput!)`.
- Mutations return a payload type with the changed entity (`SaveLocationPayload { savedLocation }`),
  never a bare boolean (except idempotent fire-and-forget like `markNotificationsRead` → `{ updatedCount }`).

## Auth scopes (default deny)
- Builder `authScopes` available: `public`, `resident`, `residentActive` (resident + terms accepted +
  ACTIVE status), and `permission: Permission` (from `src/authz/permissions.ts`).
- **Every Query/Mutation field must declare `authScopes`.** `test/schema-guard.test.ts` walks the
  schema and fails if any root field lacks it. Public fields declare `{ public: true }` explicitly.
- Object types that expose admin-only fields use field-level `authScopes` (e.g. `Correction.internalNotes`).
- Scope failures return `FORBIDDEN` (admin) or `UNAUTHENTICATED` (no principal); configure
  `unauthorizedError` in the builder to throw the catalog errors.

## Types & nullability
- IDs are `ID!` (UUID strings). Dates `DateTime` scalar (ISO-8601 UTC). URLs `URL` scalar (validated).
- Non-null by default for fields that always exist; nullable only when the data can be missing
  (e.g. `party`, `photoUrl`, `currentHolder`).
- Never expose: internal ids of other residents, emails of residents to admins, session data,
  Stripe ids, raw geometry, `source_record_url` to public (admin only), `ip_hash`.
- Civic types expose provenance: `source { name url }`, `lastUpdatedAt`, `freshness: CURRENT | MAY_BE_OUTDATED`.

## Pagination
- Relay-style connections for every list: `first: Int (≤100, default 20)`, `after: String`,
  returns `{ edges { node cursor } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } totalCount? }`. `totalCount`
  only on admin lists.
- Admin list filters are a single `filter:` input object; sort is an enum (`sort: OFFICE_SORT`).

## Resolvers
- Signature pattern:
  ```ts
  builder.mutationField('saveLocation', (t) => t.field({
    type: SaveLocationPayload,
    authScopes: { residentActive: true },
    args: { input: t.arg({ type: SaveLocationInput, required: true }) },
    resolve: (_root, { input }, ctx) => ctx.services.locations.save(ctx, input),
  }));
  ```
- No try/catch in resolvers — errors propagate to masking. No Prisma imports in `*.graphql.ts` (lint rule).
- Field resolvers that fan out use DataLoaders created per request in `context.ts`.

## Context (src/graphql/context.ts)
`{ requestId, principal, authz, services, loaders, ipHash, userAgent, reply }` — `reply` only for
setting cookies in auth-related mutations. Context is created per request; nothing request-scoped is global.
